  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,z=c.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $z$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $c$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & =c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and right to left, what are the missing parts of the derivation?",
